		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row1"><span class="name"><a name="15936"></a><b>Morani</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails">Vizier<br /><img src="images/Ranks/swords/mod6sword.gif" alt="Vizier" title="Vizier" border="0" /><br /><img src="images/avatars/9388702053ed68d7e75318.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br />Joined: 19 Aug 2002<br />Posts: 457<br />Location: Michigan, USA</span><br /></td>
		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=15936&amp;sid=710b63825cb5ce14f0ec20f321fb6abd#15936"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Wed Sep 18, 2002 10:23 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=15936&amp;sid=710b63825cb5ce14f0ec20f321fb6abd"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">“From what the young Elf has told us, I would have to agree that Fate was not on Lucan’s side.” Morani smirks a little at her understatement. “The Natural balance of life is about constant testing. The wolf tests the stag and removes those that would weaken the herd. At the same time the herd tests the wolf. If the wolf is week, either physically or mentally, it will starve or be taken down by the stag. Both keep the other strong and able to survive. If the wolf is removed; the herd will starve in the winter and be plagued with disease. If the herd is removed; the wolf will grow week and desperate and soon make a mistake that will end it. Neither the wolf or the stag can see the larger web and know it’s role with the other. We are different, we CAN see the web. So, which will you be; the predator that culls the herd, or the prey that keeps the heroes sharp?” The Ranger pauses a moment to let her words stir themselves. “I think I already know which you are, the answer is not for me anyway… Oh, and you are welcome, for both.”  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
 
<br />
Morani
<br />
Wanderer of Tunare,
<br />
Protector of The Mother's children.<i></i><br />_________________<br />Morani 
<br />
Wanderer of Tunare, 
<br />
Protector of The Mother's children.</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
